# dom_demo — DOM via wasm<->JS interop (WS3-161 / §document). EAV's DOM model
# (std/document) compiles to wasm whose ss_dom_* operations are host functions
# the JS/browser side supplies. This demo binds three such host operations
# (dom_create_node / dom_set_value / dom_get_value) as runtimeBindings: under
# `semanticscript wasm` they become wasm IMPORTS (the linker's --allow-undefined), and the
# node host provides them backed by a JS-side node map — exactly the wasm<->JS
# seam the real browser DOM adapter (ss_dom_runtime.js) uses, with a map standing
# in for `document`. main creates a node, sets its value to 42 through JS, reads
# it back through JS, and returns it; the host checks main() == 42, proving the
# DOM-interop round-trip. (A real browser would back these with document; this
# proves the codegen + interop without one.)

DomDemo is project
DomDemo module fix
DomDemo target wasm
DomDemo entry main
DomDemo platform browserWasm

fix is module
fix path fix.mod
fix exports main
fix purpose "Host the DOM wasm-interop demo entry"
fix invariant "Exposes main, which round-trips a value through JS DOM host functions"

main is operation
main out Int32
main async no
main purpose "Create a DOM node, set its value to 42 via JS, read it back, and return it"
main invariant "Returns 42 round-tripped through the JS DOM host"
main let theValue immutable Int32 42
main do makeNode
main do setNode
main do getNode
main return readBack

makeNode is call
makeNode in main
makeNode invokes document.createNode
makeNode out nodeId Int32

setNode is call
setNode in main
setNode invokes document.setValue
setNode arg node Int32 nodeId
setNode arg value Int32 theValue
setNode discards "the set-value host status is not needed"

getNode is call
getNode in main
getNode invokes document.getValue
getNode arg node Int32 nodeId
getNode out readBack Int32

browserWasm is platform
browserWasm targetRuntime wasm
browserWasm purpose "Wasm runtime platform for the DOM host adapter demo"
